# Elastic Docs — project instructions

This repository contains Elastic documentation. The following skills and tools
are available for your workflow.

## Available tools

- **Elastic Docs MCP** (`elastic-docs`, `elastic-internal-docs`): search and
  retrieve Elastic documentation pages. Use `search_docs` and
  `get_document_by_url` freely when writing or reviewing content.

## Authoring guidelines

- All pages use MyST Markdown with Elastic extensions. Run `/docs-syntax-help`
  if you are unsure about a directive.
- `applies_to` frontmatter is required on every page. Run `/applies-to-tagging`
  to validate.
- Style is enforced by Vale (Elastic rules). Run `/docs-check-style <file>` on
  any changed `.md` before committing.

## Changelogs

Changelog entries live in `<source>/.changelog/` as YAML files. Run
`/review-changelog` to audit, `/fix-changelog` to improve weak entries.

## Useful commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/docs-check-style <file>` | Vale style check |
| `/applies-to-tagging <file>` | Validate applies_to metadata |
| `/crosslink-validator <file>` | Check cross-links |
| `/frontmatter-audit <dir>` | Audit frontmatter completeness |
| `/review-changelog <file>` | Audit a changelog entry |
| `/fix-changelog <file>` | Improve a changelog entry |
| `/docs-setup` | Reconfigure the Elastic Docs Harness |
| `/docs-update` | Check and apply tool/skill updates |
